### =========================================================================
### EWMS - ATTENDANCE: CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT LOCAL REST SIMULATION
### =========================================================================
@server = http://localhost:4004
@service = odata/v4/attendance

### Seeded reference data (from db/data/*.csv, resets on every `cds deploy`)
@empJohn = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@officeShift = 20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. SELF CHECK-IN as the employee (empjohn), Office, 20 min late
###    Shift 20000000-...-01 starts 09:00, graceInMinutes: 10 -> cutoff 09:10
###    Checking in at 09:20 -> lateMinutes should be 10
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name checkIn
POST {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

{
  "employee_ID": "{{empJohn}}",
  "attendanceDate": "2026-08-10",
  "checkIn": "09:20:00",
  "workLocation": "Office"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Read it back - confirm shift_ID resolved, lateMinutes: 10,
###    attendanceStatus: "Present"
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances?$filter=employee_ID eq {{empJohn}} and attendanceDate eq 2026-08-10
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Duplicate check-in same day -> should FAIL with 400
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

{
  "employee_ID": "{{empJohn}}",
  "attendanceDate": "2026-08-10",
  "checkIn": "10:00:00"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Missing checkIn -> should FAIL with 400
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

{
  "employee_ID": "{{empJohn}}",
  "attendanceDate": "2026-08-11"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. CHECK-OUT - replace the ID below with the ID returned from step 1's
###    response (or from step 2's GET)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@attendanceId = 856a4d7d-4164-4c84-a011-c655f5d62bfb

PATCH {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances({{attendanceId}})
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

{
  "checkOut": "18:00:00"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Double checkout -> should FAIL with 400
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATCH {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances({{attendanceId}})
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

{
  "checkOut": "19:00:00"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. DELETE -> should ALWAYS FAIL with 400 (attendance is immutable)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances({{attendanceId}})
Authorization: Basic hrperson:

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. WORK-FROM-HOME self check-in, on a fresh date, on time
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

{
  "employee_ID": "{{empJohn}}",
  "attendanceDate": "2026-08-12",
  "checkIn": "09:05:00",
  "workLocation": "WorkFromHome"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. CROSS-EMPLOYEE CHECK - empjohn tries to mark attendance for someone
###    else (mgrdept's employee id below) -> should FAIL with 403
###    (self-check-in is scoped to employee_ID = $user.employeeId)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/{{service}}/Attendances
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic empjohn:

{
  "employee_ID": "10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004",
  "attendanceDate": "2026-08-12",
  "checkIn": "09:00:00"
}























